  "name": "qubrics-token-efficient-usage",
  "description": "Use when the question is about *how to call* Qubrics cheaply, not what to send: choosing batch vs. looped sends, mailbox search/count/batch-read vs. full fetches, sync deltas, cursor pagination, ETags/conditional requests, idempotency keys, or picking between MCP, the qubrics CLI, an SDK, or direct HTTP. Trigger for reducing token/round-trip/API-call cost, avoiding broad mailbox or log fetches, or optimising a polling/sync loop.\\n\\nThis is a routing/cost-decision skill, never a content-authoring one. If the request asks to write, draft, compose, or format the actual JSON body, subject, text, or attachment bytes of an email — even a single email, even one with an attachment, even inside a larger batch — do NOT use this skill; route that to qubrics-send-email or qubrics-attachments instead. Ask yourself: is the user asking \"what's the cheapest way to call Qubrics,\" or \"what should this email/attachment contain\"? Only the former belongs here.",
